# The tla-kit image TOPAK's TLA+ checks run in, by the digest tla-kit's release workflow published (ADR-0077 §1,
# Proposed). One line per field, `key value`, in the form of tools/TLAPS-PIN. tools/check-pins.sh checks that
# jar_sha256 is tools/TLA-PIN's jar, and reports tlapm_sha256 against tools/TLAPS-PIN until that pin names this
# image (ADR-0077 §5). .github/workflows/results.yml verifies the image's attestations before any job uses it, and
# runs the tlc and proofs jobs in it. tla-kit's CONSUMERS.md names this file; its log of each project's pin is made
# there, by tla-kit's custodian. This repository sends nothing there.
